WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.150
- I've gotta be honest.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.041
We can be shallow AF.

00:00:05.041 --> 00:00:07.014
(laughing)
- Yes!

00:00:07.014 --> 00:00:07.847
So shallow!

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:09.973
(laughing)

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:11.930
(dramatic music)

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.950
- [Narrator] Jubilee presents: "Spectrum",

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.907
season five, episode five; "Blind People."

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.210
We invited six blind people

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.153
to see the range of their
beliefs and experiences.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.590
- Hey, I'm Alisha, and I'm 31.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.370
I live in Toronto currently,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.300
and I was diagnosed 10 years
ago as Stargardt's disease.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.060
- I'm Christine Ha, I'm in
Houston, Texas, United States.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.910
I'm best known for winning
"Master Chef", season three.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.016
- Hi, I'm James Rath.

00:00:43.016 --> 00:00:44.880
I'm legally blind since birth,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.330
and I'm currently in
Los Angeles, California.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.300
- I'm Lucy Edwards.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.980
I'm 24, and I'm based
in the United Kingdom,

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.520
and I'm best known for being
the first ever blind presenter

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.310
on BBC Radio One, and I'm also a YouTuber.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.070
- I'm Mario Bonds, I'm based in Maryland.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.490
I am best known from season
two of "The Glee Project,

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:07.200
and the PBS documentary, "Blind Love."

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.560
- Hi, I'm Molly Burke.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.030
I'm 26 years old, in
Los Angeles, California.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.670
I have retinitis pigmentosa
and I'm a YouTuber,

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.200
motivational speaker,
and commercial model.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.410
- [Narrator] The first prompt is:

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.090
Being blind has enhanced my other senses.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.150
Alisha.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.340
- Somewhat agree.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.420
- [Narrator] Christine.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.800
- Somewhat agree.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:29.760
- [Narrator] James.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.730
- Somewhat agree.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.660
- [Narrator] Lucy.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.740
- Disagree.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.780
- [Narrator] Mario.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.000
- Strongly agree.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:35.833
- [Narrator] Molly.

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:36.666
- Agree.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.740
A lot of commentors say,
oh, are you Daredevil?

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.220
And I think I just want to
smash this misconception.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.710
We don't have like
supersonic other senses.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:48.570
- Yes.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.970
The misconception that
we're somehow superhuman,

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.570
that drives me nuts.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.500
But I think, if I leave out of my house,

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.340
and I've ordered an Uber,
I know my driveway, right?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.570
So when I walk out of my
house, I'm totally blind.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.650
But immediately my ears say,

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.410
okay, there's the engine of the car.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:07.790
I hear the incidental click
of the doors unlocking,

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.690
and I instantly know

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.700
where to reach out and
grab the door handle,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.050
and of course to the driver,

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.376
they don't know a blind
person just got in their car.

00:02:15.376 --> 00:02:17.300
(laughing)
- Yeah.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.850
- I said somewhat agree because

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.570
it's more so that I pay
attention to things more.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.770
So I don't think necessarily
that you get heightened senses.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.770
It's more so that you have
to depend on your other four

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.280
senses when you lose your vision.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.020
- I said I agree because

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.540
I lost the majority of my vision at 14,

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.333
I've been legally blind from birth.

00:02:37.503 --> 00:02:39.200
And when I lost my vision,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.590
I immediately struggled to
adapt to my other senses.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:44.530
I really struggled with taste.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.600
I had to eliminate things like
garlic, onion, spicy foods.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.720
I also struggled with smell a lot.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.450
I would distinctly remember
being in a restaurant,

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.130
and they burnt cheese, and I
had to leave the restaurant.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.520
This was the same year I went blind.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.500
So for me, that was like a truly immediate

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.810
heightening of my senses,

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.250
but things like my hearing and my touch,

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.670
I would say are more based
on paying more attention.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.370
- [Narrator] Next prompt is:

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:13.870
I prefer to date fellow blind people.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.313
- Ooh.

00:03:15.313 --> 00:03:18.200
(laughing)

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.200
- [Narrator] Alisha.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.150
- Disagree.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.340
- [Narrator] Christine.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.770
- I disagree.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:23.603
- [Narrator] James.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.570
- Disagree.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:25.550
- [Narrator] Lucy.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.690
- Disagree.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:27.610
- [Narrator] Mario.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.650
- Disagree.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:29.580
- [Narrator] Molly.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.793
- Somewhat disagree.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.720
- I've been told that I'm
a pretty beautiful man.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.240
So I need to have somebody keep telling me

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.087
that I still have myself together.

00:03:37.087 --> 00:03:39.120
(laughing)

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.397
It's important people to know,

00:03:40.397 --> 00:03:41.800
just because we are
blind, doesn't mean that

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.590
we're automatically gonna
have a blind partner.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.380
We live in the freedom of love
coming in whatever condition

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.930
or situation it may be in.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.900
- I'm currently married
to someone who is sighted.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.733
When I think about it,

00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:55.870
I'm like, life is easier
because he can drive me around,

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.730
or tell me if like a certain
ingredient is expired in the

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.670
pantry, ever tell me if
I have food in my teeth.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.700
- I said somewhat disagree,

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.550
because I don't prefer to date somebody

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.910
who is or who isn't.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.760
I'm currently in a relationship
with a blind person.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.790
Prior to this, my partner
has only dated sighted women,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.410
and I've only dated sighted men.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.610
I don't care that neither of us can drive,

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.970
'cause we can still get around.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.250
I don't care that he can't
see some of the things that I

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.780
can't either, because we
can find ways around that,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.490
like using apps, like "Be My Eyes",

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.630
With my sighted partners in the past,

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.410
there was only so much
understanding they could have

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.430
of my lived experience daily.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:37.580
Whereas every day now, I get
to come home to a partner that

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.390
completely understands my life experience.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:42.890
Me and Ollie have a
little bit of a different

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.130
sort of love story.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.130
I saw him before I went blind.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.260
I went blind two months
into our relationship.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.120
So this may sound controversial,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.450
but I feel like he lived
my blindness with me.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.360
He felt all of the emotions that I felt

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.340
as a 17 year old girl,

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.330
feeling alone and having
this loss and grief.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:08.330
My sighted partner understands me as Lucy,

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.790
and understands me as a blind woman,

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:16.790
way deeper than I could ever
find in any blind partner,

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.180
just because of what we've
lived through together.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:22.160
So we're getting married
next year, so yay!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.350
- Woo-hoo!
- Congratulations.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.900
- Thank you.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.870
- [Narrator] I'd love to ask
a follow-up question too.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.550
People were curious, are
blind people less shallow

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.700
about romantic partners?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.360
- Oh!
- Oh.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.680
- Love this question, love it.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.610
- I've gotta be honest.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.753
We can be shallow AF.

00:05:42.904 --> 00:05:44.099
- Yeah.
(laughing)

00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:46.580
- Yes, so shallow!

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.560
- One of the first things
I'm gonna notice is,

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:49.500
what does your voice sound like?

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.430
- Exactly.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.220
- Hair is a massive thing for me.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.600
I love when Ollie has his
hair cut, I love his beard.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.960
- I noticed the feel of nice hands

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.530
the same way a sighted person
would notice pretty eyes.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:03.210
- Smell, smell, smell is so big.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.480
- Oh yeah, smell.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.657
- I get the sense of feeling.

00:06:05.657 --> 00:06:07.140
- Cologne's gotta be right.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.450
- You know how like, girls are like,

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:09.790
are you into arms or abs?

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:10.623
Like, I've always been like,

00:06:10.623 --> 00:06:13.200
I'm an arms girl, because
it's the first impression

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.033
I have of a man.

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.160
When he gives me sighted guide, I'm like,

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.920
but how's that arm hair situation?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.360
How's that arm fitness?

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.453
Like, what's that like,
you know, bicep like?

00:06:20.453 --> 00:06:24.440
Like I get my full scope of
his, you know, his make-up.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.800
- And there've been times where, you know,

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:26.633
the whole side of her was like,

00:06:26.633 --> 00:06:28.450
oh, she doesn't look like
she belongs with you,

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.600
but I did not care because
it's what I found to be

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.560
attractive both by virtue of
personality and what she felt

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.430
like to me and everything
like that was fine.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.030
- I am as shallow as my sighted friends,

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.440
it's just in different ways.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.800
I do still experience physical
and sexual attraction,

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.750
like any sighted person would, and so yes,

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:52.730
I do have preferences of
height, of hair, of body type,

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.010
- Oh, I would say the opposite,

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.070
being legally blind actually,

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.690
because I've been going
through the degeneration

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.530
of my eye disease for the last 10 years.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:03.340
Like I was diagnosed when I
was 21, and back then I had

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.730
different preferences for
what I was looking for,

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.280
and now my preferences are more lifelong.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.220
Like is this person gonna stay by me

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.520
as my vision degenerates?

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.430
And because of that, I
don't look so much at

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.760
what they look like,
because I can't see them

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.620
as well as I used to, but
also because I need to know

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.770
that they match me inside.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.210
- [Narrator] Unsolicited
help makes things harder.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.880
- I would say, somewhat agree.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.420
- I'm also somewhat agree.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.460
- Strongly agree.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.670
- Somewhat agree.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:31.780
- Somewhat agree.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:32.763
- Somewhat agree.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:36.100
- This happened the other day at the mall.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.330
And especially in a post pandemic world,

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:42.090
I don't necessarily want
people getting up in my space.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.020
And it's hard to sort of police that

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.430
as a blind person sometimes.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.660
I had a security guard just
literally take hold of me.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.960
He didn't even know where I was going.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.210
Then I told him and then like,

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.290
I know where I am and I just
wasn't really comfortable

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:54.123
with that scenario.

00:07:54.123 --> 00:07:56.880
And then I've had past scenarios
where I've actually been

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.100
literally guided into traffic.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:00.890
It was kind of a scary scenario,

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.380
and it just all happened so fast.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.360
I really didn't know how to react.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.210
- I've been in situations
where I've actually been

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.790
cursed out for refusing help.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:08.880
"I'll get the door for you."

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.730
"Oh no, please don't, I have it."

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:11.230
"No, I'll get the door for you."

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:13.020
"Oh no, I'm fine, I'm fine, I have it."

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.180
"I'll get the door for
you", "oh no, I'm fine."

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.340
"Damn, I was just trying
to help your blind ass."

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.650
- Whoa.
- It was almost like

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:21.160
as if I robbed them of a Cub Scout moment,

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.380
but it's more of a respect thing.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.800
- I totally agree with you, Mario.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:28.300
I've got Google maps in my
bone conducting headphones,

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.060
and I'm with Olga, my guide dog, you know,

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.410
I know where I'm going.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:36.620
There's a lady who stroked Olga
as I was crossing the road.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.150
There's cars coming and
you're just like, wow,

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.840
like where am I, what am I doing?

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:43.160
Then obviously Olga's distracted.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.590
Then you're a bit off whack.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:49.450
And I think the motto here
should be just ask, don't grab.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.420
Just come up to me and say,
you know, "You look lost."

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.403
"I'm Sally. I'm a passer-by."

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.410
"You look like you need help."

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.110
"Do you need any assistance?"

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:02.590
And then that gives the
autonomy back to us and to say,

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:04.300
actually, yeah, I would really love it.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.900
Or actually, no, I don't
need help right now.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.550
- So I chose somewhat agree

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:12.550
for a different reason,
being as I don't look blind.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:14.170
When I look at unsolicited help,

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.980
I think of it as advice,
they tend to give me advice.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:19.640
Like, you know, maybe
you just shouldn't work,

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.800
because this is too much work for you.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:24.250
It doesn't boost the morale,
it doesn't actually help,

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.630
and it actually hinders
and makes me feel like,

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:29.470
you don't see me as
capable and independent.

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:31.480
- I said, somewhat agree.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.050
I don't always know that I need help.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.090
So sometimes unsolicited advice or help

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:42.090
is actually really beneficial
for me, but overwhelmingly,

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:45.060
I generally will ask for
help if I do need it.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.900
You know, we have our process.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:49.370
I might have to sit through, you know,

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.630
three cycles of traffic at an intersection

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.780
if I've never crossed out
that intersection before,

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:54.960
but I'm not lost.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.900
I'm just doing what I need to do

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.410
to be safe and to
accommodate my disability,

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:02.220
and I think all of us like
to have as much independence,

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.330
as much freedom as we can have.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.100
And so sometimes interrupting

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:09.260
us having independence and
freedom, can be frustrating.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:12.370
And it does feel like you're
underestimating our ability.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:14.010
- I will say though, that I appreciate it

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.110
if my husband tells me my
cane's about to go into

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:18.010
dog poo or something.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.260
- Fair enough, fair enough.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.640
- Well, yeah.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:21.473
That's my foot.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.440
Unwanted perfume.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:28.070
- [Narrator] The city I live
in is easily accessible for me.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.480
- Somewhat disagree.

