00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:04.110
whereas like these wider spread
cities that depend a lot on

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:06.960
cars getting to get
around like LA or Houston

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.710
seems to be less accessible.

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.875
- As a blind individual,

00:13:10.875 --> 00:13:14.245
I ended up paying a fortune
when I want to be independent.

00:13:14.245 --> 00:13:16.690
I ended up paying a fortune
in transportation costs.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.450
You know, I look at it like this,

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:21.000
at any time I want to leave the house,

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:24.240
it costs me a coin, so to speak.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.640
- And not only is it often, you know,

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.100
more expensive to be blind

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.250
because we do have to pay higher rent

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.520
to live in these more
accessible neighborhoods,

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.070
and just accessible technology

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.520
and all of these extra costs in our lives.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:40.990
But also many blind people live in poverty

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:43.280
due to lack of job opportunities.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:44.990
So not only is it more expensive,

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:47.330
you know, we're lower income, overall.

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:49.530
- Yeah, the huge point, you know,

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.500
80% of working age blind
adults are unemployed,

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.230
and that the statistics
that have risen steadily

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:57.150
since the 1970s, so that's
a really good point.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:58.840
